  "description": "A parametric RUG on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nSPACE-HOSTED AND FITTED BY DEFAULT. A rug belongs to a room, so this one ships with Fit to host on Max and a 400 mm margin: drop it on a Space and it lands centred with a border of floor showing, which is what a rug is for. Every other object in this library ships with fit Off, because every other object has a size of its own; a rug's size is the room's.\n\nTHE BORDER IS FOUR BARS AROUND A FIELD, not a rectangle with a thicker line. That is what lets the field and the border carry different colours and different published areas — and the field area, not the rug area, is the figure that matters when the border is 120 mm and the rug is 2.4 m.\n\nTHREE SHAPES. Rectangular and Runner are the same construction with the width pinched to 35% of the length; Round abandons the quad table for a 36-point ring, and empties the border and fringe with it — a round rug with a mitred border would be a lie about how rugs are made.",
